                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "62db4d50-acc1-3367-bd10-c673ef5344a2",
                                        "entry_id": "ee07e1db-fcd2-3310-ab97-7c8cd3784ae7",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A carpenter bee."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4d1307e9-857b-43a9-adbe-5b82c8e46108",
                                                "sense_id": "62db4d50-acc1-3367-bd10-c673ef5344a2",
                                                "text": "The large, stout African bees are carpenters (Xylocopa), making small tunnels in timber, housing few individuals."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "66b6a45d-643e-3da1-a77e-11609e189490",
                                        "entry_id": "ee07e1db-fcd2-3310-ab97-7c8cd3784ae7",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A woodlouse."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "British",
                                            "Canada",
                                            "regional"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6970fbf9-97d4-4f69-8da8-abd2a8e1ea74",
                                                "sense_id": "66b6a45d-643e-3da1-a77e-11609e189490",
                                                "text": "Eleven names in Laver’s table (just over 6%) are of the “carpenter” type, a name for woodlice also recorded in Shropshire and Warwickshire.[…] Apparently a Newfoundland word for woodlouse is “carpenter” or “cafner” (another is also “boat-builder”). These names clearly relate to the animals’ affinity to wood as will “carpenter’s flea”, “wood-pig”, “wood-bug”, “grampus wood-bug” and, of course “woodlouse”."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
